WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.309
As a gangly kid who had just arrived

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.049
in the U.S. from Cameroon, 16

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:05.669
year-old Joel Embiid had a lot of

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:06.959
the gifts that he'd eventually put

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.159
to use in the NBA.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.049
The height, the athleticism, that

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:11.909
massive seven foot six

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:13.619
wingspan. But the one thing that he

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.659
couldn't do was actually shoot

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:16.649
a basketball.

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.089
Embiid didn't get into the game at

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:19.979
all until he was about 15.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.959
Today he has become not just

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.369
the linchpin of a championship

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.109
chasing team in Philadelphia.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:26.909
He's also arguably the best

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.919
basketball player on the planet

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.659
and he was recently named the NBA's

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.399
Most Valuable Player for the current

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:32.422
season.

00:00:32.423 --> 00:00:33.423
2023 MVP

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:37.330
from the Philadelphia 76ers.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:41.439
It's possible that this never would

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:42.969
have happened if it weren't for

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:44.889
YouTube. In a 2016 interview

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:46.389
with Sports Illustrated Embiid

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:48.489
shared the secret to his success

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:49.989
learning to shoot long distance

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:52.419
shots by watching, in his words,

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.429
videos of regular white

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:55.779
people on the Internet.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:57.609
When you want to when you look at

00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:59.709
the best shooters of all time,

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:00.710
you know there is a common,

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:03.399
there is a common theme.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.259
She is going to be in the shooting

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:05.739
mode.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:07.359
So basically the idea is most

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:08.769
players, when they shoot, they set

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:10.149
the ball up here on their shoulder.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:11.379
Footwork is our foundation.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:12.369
Footwork is everything.

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:13.809
We're stepping into our shot.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:15.699
Yes, Embiid is a big dude,

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.469
but there are a lot of those in the

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:19.389
NBA. What sets him apart is

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:20.889
his ability to do more than just

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:23.079
stand under the basket and dunk.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:24.909
For a seven-footer, he's got an

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:26.889
incredibly efficient jump shot.

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:28.569
During his career, Embiid has sunk

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:30.609
more than 33% of his three

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:31.839
point attempts.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:33.339
Now no one's going to confuse him

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:34.929
with Steph Curry, but that's a

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:36.669
better shooting percentage than

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:37.659
Michael Jordan.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.288
And it's miles ahead of other guys

00:01:39.289 --> 00:01:41.289
Embiid's size, most

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:43.359
of whom hardly ever score that far

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:44.289
from the basket.

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.599
And for that, he credits YouTube.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:48.609
Now you and I are unlikely to become

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:50.199
professional basketball players by

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.939
watching hours of white dudes

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.739
shooting three pointers tonight.

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:55.269
Sorry. But you might learn how to

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:57.399
repair a leaky toilet or install

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:58.809
a utility sink in your basement by

00:01:58.810 --> 00:01:59.889
watching YouTube.

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:00.699
I did.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:02.559
Every day, untold numbers

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.209
of people are accomplishing less

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:05.799
audacious tasks because of the

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.779
knowledge that others make freely

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:09.579
available via all sorts of online

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.439
platforms from Wikipedia to Tik

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.539
Tok. The incredible amount

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:14.949
of free knowledge that's available

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:16.929
online is staggering,

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:19.209
and that knowledge confers agency

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:21.399
on anyone who's willing to use it.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.629
Are there cranks on YouTube

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:24.339
spreading silly conspiracies and

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:26.259
crazy uncles on Facebook sharing Q

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:27.159
and on memes?

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.139
Of course, when politicians

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:30.549
call for regulating social media and

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.409
other online platforms, they risk

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:34.149
throwing out a lot of the good with

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:35.019
the bad.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.279
Often in the name of protecting

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:37.839
children, they ought to consider the

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.489
other side of that equation too.

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:41.529
Being exposed to unfamiliar ideas

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:43.509
can sometimes be scary, but

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:45.339
like it was for 16 year-old

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:47.079
Joel Embiid trying to refine his

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.879
untapped athletic potential.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:50.620
It can also be game changing.

